course: dictionary
lesson: 7450
title: Pony
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pony is a kind of small horse. It stays small even when it is fully grown, so it is smaller than most horses. Many children learn to ride on ponies at riding schools and pony clubs.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Ponies are small horses, usually under about 1.47 metres at the shoulder, often from cold hilly places like Shetland, Wales or Dartmoor.» The size and the hilly places tell you what a pony is like.
explain: Some people use pony in a looser, everyday way, for any horse that children ride. This is informal, so you will hear it in talk more than in science books. Always check the sentence: does it mean a tiny horse, or a horse a child rides?
fact: A pony is a small horse that stays small when fully grown.
fact: «Shetland pony» is a type of pony, named after the Shetland Islands.
fact: Ponies are often strong for their size: «For its size a Shetland pony is one of the strongest horses.»
fact: Ponies often have thick coats to keep out wind and rain, so some hardy ponies need no rug in winter.
fact: «Ponytail» is a different word: it means hair tied back, not a small horse.
exercise: What is a pony? | A cat with a long tail | A big farm animal that pulls ploughs | *A kind of small horse that stays small when fully grown | A horse that is very old
exercise: «Ponies have thick coats for wind and rain.» What does thick tell you about a pony's coat? | *Lots of hair, good for keeping warm | Very thin and see-through | Cut very short | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «Lena tied her hair back in a ponytail.» What does ponytail mean? | A pony club rule | *Hair tied back at the back of the head | A horse's tail painted red | A horse with a long mane
test: «Riders wear helmets on every horse, even a quiet pony, because any horse may spook at a bag or a bird.» What does spook mean? | Turn into a pony | Fall fast asleep | Run very slowly | *Suddenly take fright
test: Informally, pony is a word some people use for what? | *A horse that children ride | A large horse that pulls carts only | A wild bird from the moors | A donkey with long ears
exam: «Some horses need rugs in winter, while hardy ponies grow thick coats and may need no rug at all.» Why might a hardy pony need no rug? | *Its thick coat keeps it warm | It only lives in summer | Rugs are only for wild horses | It is too small to wear one
